10. Conclusion

We have presented a unified normative theory in which all cognitive operations are governed by Future Value maximization. The framework rests on a rigorous semi‑Markov foundation, with essential proofs of contraction, necessity, regret decomposition, and error propagation. Under a generic non‑degeneracy condition, hierarchical composition inevitably produces genuinely novel operations, offering a principled route to open‑ended cognitive development in AI. By unifying perception, reasoning, and memory, the theory provides a coherent blueprint for building adaptive agents whose cognitive repertoire expands autonomously and efficiently.

